# fleet-pulse identity is PER-MACHINE and must never be shared. ~/.config/systemd
# is a whole-directory symlink into this repo, so a drop-in written at runtime
# lands here rather than staying local. fleet-pulse.service itself is tracked and
# identical everywhere; the drop-in is what says WHICH machine this is. Commit one
# and every box that pulls it starts reporting under that name - the desktop would
# claim the laptop's key, which is the collision the separate keys exist to prevent.
.config/systemd/user/fleet-pulse.service.d/
# personal notes/agent systemd units (+ their .target.wants symlinks), both levels
.config/systemd/user/*notes*
.config/systemd/user/*agentctl*
.config/systemd/user/*git-sync*
.config/systemd/user/*journal*
.config/systemd/user/*inbox*
.config/systemd/user/*mqtt*
.config/systemd/user/*regen-project*
.config/systemd/user/*lab-sync*
.config/systemd/user/*/*notes*
.config/systemd/user/*/*agentctl*
.config/systemd/user/*/*git-sync*
.config/systemd/user/*/*journal*
.config/systemd/user/*/*inbox*
.config/systemd/user/*/*mqtt*
.config/systemd/user/*/*regen-project*
.config/systemd/user/*/*lab-sync*

# Agent runtime state — lives in the standalone ~/.agent repo, never tracked here
.agent/

# Test suite: vendored bats + per-run failure artifacts (see tests/Makefile bootstrap)
# Trailing slash would match only a real directory. A git worktree needs `tests/vendor`
# SYMLINKED to the primary checkout's copy (bootstrap clones it once), and a symlink is
# not a directory -- so the slash form left it showing as untracked in every worktree,
# one `git add .` away from being committed.
tests/vendor
tests/vendor/
tests/artifacts/

# Python bytecode. `python3 -m py_compile` on any tracked script (claude-recall,
# for one) drops these next to the source, where a `git add -A` will sweep them up.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# theme-switch OUTPUT. These three files are generated in full -- kitty and
# waybar are copied verbatim from `.local/src/theme/templates/<tool>/<theme>`,
# sketchybar's colors.sh is a heredoc built from `palettes/<theme>.sh`. The
# tracked source of truth is the palette + template; these are the render.
#
# They were tracked for years, and the theme-day/theme-night systemd timers
# rewrite them at 07:00 and 19:00 DAILY -- so the repo dirtied itself twice a
# day forever and every session had to decide to hold the churn. A generator
# aimed at its own source is not mess to sweep, it is a loop to cut.
#
# A fresh clone has none of these files, and sketchybarrc hard-`source`s
# colors.sh -- so the installer's setup_theme() renders them at install time.
.config/kitty/current-theme.conf
.config/waybar/style.css
.config/sketchybar/colors.sh
